            "secret:kbclan": "Does real work in your team's apps with its own credentials",
            "secret:1lrxb1u": "Gathers context continuously and remembers what it learns",
            "secret:yydody": "Works as proactively as you want, staying in the background by default",
            "secret:1ecdzyz": "Usage for Claude Tag only · Expires {date} · Terms apply",
            "secret:1lycmb1": "Usage for Claude Tag only · Expires {date}",
            "secret:1i4ln4g": "Set up Claude Tag",
            "secret:10vpbd6": "Learn more",
            "secret:nnx38p": "Set up Claude Tag",
            "secret:pyk2sg": "Bring Claude into your Slack channels. Anyone on your team can <strong>@Claude</strong> and Claude answers using the tools you connect, from BigQuery to GitHub.",
            "secret:gev4mg": "What to expect",
            "secret:nlvk2o": "First {amount} of usage on us",
            "secret:nnuhug": "Terms apply",
            "secret:nnjxkj": "Start setup",
            "secret:ma2dj0": "Resume setup",
            "secret:1p504lu": "FAQs",
            "secret:jh1irp": "What can Claude see in Slack?",
            "secret:jh1idx": "Claude reads messages in the channels it's in, including any it's not tagged in. When someone asks it to search or do research, Claude can also look across your workspace's public channels, the same way any member could. Claude can't see into a private channel from outside it—what's said there is visible to Claude only in that channel. For conversations in a private channel, Claude is not allowed to post outside of the channel.",
            "secret:jh1irq": "Does Claude respond only when someone tags it?",
            "secret:jh1idy": "Claude will reply when someone tags it in a channel. It also follows the conversation between tags, and may sometimes join in untagged when it thinks it can help. If you'd rather Claude stay quiet until tagged, you can tell it so for each channel.",
            "secret:jh1irr": "Does Claude Tag use my accounts to do its work?",
            "secret:jh1idz": "<p>No. In channels, Claude uses its own account in each tool, set up by you here. Everything it does shows up as Claude—not as you or whoever set it up—and you control what those accounts can reach.</p><p>GitHub is the one exception to the pattern: you sign in with your own GitHub account once to authorize your GitHub organization and install the Claude GitHub App. Then you choose exactly which repositories Claude can use.</p>",
            "secret:jh1irs": "Can Claude Tag use the connectors we've already set up in Claude?",
            "secret:jh1ie0": "No. Connectors in someone's own Claude settings are personal—they act as that person and work only for them. In a Slack channel, everyone works with the same Claude, so it needs shared tools with accounts of its own, and you connect those here. You'll set up each tool once for your organization, even if people already use it in their own Claude.",
            "secret:jh1irt": "Who can set this up?",
            "secret:jh1ie1": "<p>Two roles are involved. On the Slack side, a Slack workspace admin or owner connects Claude to your workspace. On the Claude side, an owner of your Claude workspace sets up Claude's tools and access here.</p><p>Some steps can involve other people too. Connecting GitHub requires someone who manages your GitHub organization. And for other tools, you can send a link to whoever on your team holds that tool's credentials—they don't need to be a Claude workspace owner, and you approve what they add.</p>",
            "secret:jh1iru": "How much does this cost?",
            "secret:jh1ie2": "<p>Claude Tag is available on Team and Enterprise plans, and it's billed by usage—you pay for the work Claude does, not per seat.{hasPromo, select, true { Your first {amount} is free until {date}.} other {}}</p><p>Work Claude does in channels is billed to your organization. When someone messages Claude in a DM instead, that usage counts against their own Claude limits, not your organization's Claude Tag usage.</p>",
            "secret:jh1irv": "What happens if we hit our spend limit?",
            "secret:jh1ie3": "<p>Claude stops taking on new work in Slack and says so in the channel. It will start responding again when your spend limit resets at the start of the next month, or if you raise the limit.</p><p>You'll be alerted as you approach your spend limit. If you don't set a limit, there's no cap at all.{hasPromo, select, true { When your free usage runs out or expires, billing starts. Until then, your spend stays at {zero}.} other {}}</p>",
            "secret:jh1irw": "Can we choose which model Claude Tag uses?",
            "secret:jh1ie4": "Yes. You can set the model Claude uses in these settings—for the whole workspace or for specific channels. People in Slack can't switch models themselves, so whatever you choose here is what everyone gets.",
            "secret:jh1irx": "Is our Slack data used to train models?",
            "secret:jh1ie5": "No. Conversations with Claude Tag aren't used to train our models. They're also kept separate from people's own Claude accounts—what happens in Slack doesn't appear in anyone's Claude history, and conversations people have with Claude elsewhere don't appear in Slack.",
            "secret:d8rvip": "Pair your Slack workspace",
            "secret:6nbw0e": "Choose Claude's first tools",
            "secret:8k57yy": "Connect GitHub",
            "secret:1pkih0d": "Claude works in tools with its own account, so it can act as itself, not you.",
            "secret:1h150wf": "Recommended",
            "secret:ne1jcv": "Search all tools",
            "secret:1xv13qw": "<strong>How is this different from connectors?</strong> Connectors in your Claude account are personal to you. Claude signs into its own tools and everything it does is recorded under its name.",
            "secret:12nat1g": "Next: Connect GitHub",
            "secret:h1s346": "Next: Choose your GitHub repos",
